{"school":{"dbn":"10X091","name":"P.S. 091 Bronx","boro":"Bronx","district":"10","district_label":"District 10","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Elementary","grades":"K-5","status":"open","enrollment":354,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"2200 AQUEDUCT AVENUE, BRONX, NY 10453","phone":"718-584-5805","website":"PS91X.ORG","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/kindergarten/70725","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"P.S. 91 is a Performing Arts Elementary School in the University Heights section of the Bronx serving approximately 360 students in grades K-5. Principal Nasjletti has been leading the school for 15 years.  It is presently a school in good standing in terms of NYSED accountability. We provide General Education, Special Education (ICT, Self-Contained, and Horizon), English as a New Language (ENL), and Bilingual classroom settings. We provide mandated services that include ENL support, counseling, SETSS, occupational therapy, physical therapy, and mono and bilingual speech therapy. Student attendance is our top priority. The school's attendance goal is to reach 100%.\n\nSPECIAL INITIATIVES: \n\nARTS: We are very proud of our ever-growing Arts program. We offer classes in visual and performing arts, including music, art, theater, and dance.  Our certified music teacher organizes concerts in the Winter and Spring that are enjoyed by the entire school community, including parents and elected officials. Our certified art teacher provides instruction in art which includes painting, drawing, designing, and photography. Our Arts program is also supported by outside partnerships including  dancing Classrooms, Jazz at Lincoln Center, Rosie\u00c3\u00a2\u00c2\u0080\u00c2\u0099s Theater Kids, Young People's Chorus of NYC, and Materials for the Arts. These art programs have had a positive impact on parental involvement and increased the opportunities to invite parents into our school. Besides the Arts, we offer academic,  chess, soccer, and basketball after-school programs. The Autism Horizon Program supports students with autism in a special class with eight students, a special education teacher and paraprofessional with emphasis on building skills and offering opportunities for meaningful inclusion in larger settings. Students in this program may need additional academic support and require speech and language services, including in areas of social or pragmatic communication. For more information, speak with your CSE or IEP team and refer to Specialized Programs for Students with Disabilities (nyc.gov).","start_time":null,"end_time":null,"languages":null,"subway":"4 to 183rd St; B, D to 182nd-183rd Sts","bus":"Bx1, Bx12, Bx12-SBS, Bx2, Bx3, Bx32, Bx36, Bx40, Bx42, BxM3, BxM4","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":null,"latitude":40.857944,"longitude":-73.907798,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.892],"st":["ok"],"n":[43.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.913,0.917,0.906,0.866,0.894,0.901,0.894],"st":["ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok"],"n":[707.0,663.0,554.0,497.0,444.0,400.0,402.0],"c":[null,null,null,null,null,0.869,0.874]},"attendance_remote_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.907],"st":["ok"],"n":[550.0]},"chronic_absent_ems_all":{"y":["2015-16","2016-17","2017-18","2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.677,0.667,0.678,0.651,0.696,0.685,0.444,0.555,0.576,0.56],"st":["ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok"],"n":[790.0,805.0,793.0,696.0,628.0,543.0,477.0,427.0,394.0,398.0],"c":[0.706,0.707,0.705,0.719,null,null,null,0.573,0.578,0.6],"s":[2.45,1.09,2.03,1.89,null,null,null,2.8,2.95,2.63],"b":["below","low","below","low",null,null,null,"below","below","below"]},"chronic_absent_ems_allea":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2024-25"],"v":[0.92,0.857,0.875,0.688